FINDINGS (for the lead's backlog; none is an RF3 contract failure)
  F1 (criterion 6, brief premise). GET /insights/recurring does NOT render the "About
     these estimates" fold. That route renders the separate `insights-recurring-partial`
     define, which on master already carries its own DIFFERENTLY-WORDED, still-visible
     caveat ("Estimates through 2026-08-27, ... Totals sum displayed estimates. Monthly
     and annual figures are rounded separately.") and has no "Retained estimates:" line
     at all (grep -c 'Retained estimates' = 0, 'About these estimates' = 0 in the
     branch response). RF3 spec C names `#insights-recurring` in pages/insights.html
     only, so the fold contract does not reach this define. The partial's ONLY
     branch-vs-master delta is RF3's type bumps inside `insights-recurring-group`
     (h3 text-base->text-lg, p text-sm->text-base on the three group headers; money
     strings $183.82/$2,205.77, $835.64/$10,027.56, $6,784.18/$81,410.35 unchanged).
     Net effect: the same caveat is folded on /insights and visible on
     /insights/recurring. The route is reachable only via cmd/validate; no template
     hx-get targets it.
  F2 (spec RF3 B). "sentence <p> in ... Recurring headers text-sm -> text-base" was not
     applied in #insights-recurring: the visible "Retained estimates:" line renders as
     `<p class="text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">`, and both folded sentences
     are text-sm. The What-changed and Review headers WERE bumped (verified text-base
     in the rendered page). Type-scale conformance is the a11y lane's call; recorded
     here as a factual deviation from B.
  F3 (contract wording, introduced by the spec's own "move verbatim" instruction). The
     moved sentence still reads "Each finding below is tied to an actual transaction",
     but the fold now sits AFTER the findings list, not before it (measured index in
     #insights-findings: BRANCH sentence 40343 vs list 436 -> AFTER; MASTER sentence
     473 vs list 664 -> BEFORE). With 0 findings there is also nothing "below". The
     worker followed spec C exactly; the wording fix is a lead decision.
  F4 (progressive enhancement, contract-compliant). With JS disabled the "Show all 41
     categories" button renders and is inert — all 41 rows are already visible and the
     control does nothing. Spec D mandates the server-rendered button with no `hidden`,
     so this is per contract, but it is a misleading affordance in the JS-off path.

